  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Exhaustion, broken sleep and low mood for about two months, under sustained threats and a punishing schedule, after an admission for exhaustion and a respiratory infection six months ago; cause not established at intake: a depressive disorder, an adjustment disorder, PTSD, an insomnia disorder, thyroid disease and anemia to be assessed; psychiatry consultation requested</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R53.83</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented admission for exhaustion and the threats against him; superseded by the diagnoses at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate (DSM-5-TR), arising under chronic threat, surveillance and overwork; no suicidal ideation; PTSD not present on screening and interview</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F32.1</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the psychiatry consultation, linked to his documented exhaustion and threats and to biographers&apos; accounts of depression (R); not a claim that he was so diagnosed.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Insomnia disorder (DSM-5-TR), comorbid with depression: trouble falling and staying asleep at least four nights a week for over three months, with short sleep from late-night work and travel</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>G47.00</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the psychiatry consultation.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Nicotine dependence, cigarettes: about a pack a day since his twenties, smoked out of public view</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F17.210</td><td>S — Synthetic modern problem anchored to the documented account of his heavy, hidden smoking.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Elevated blood pressure readings in the clinic (138/88 mmHg) without a diagnosis of hypertension; home monitoring to confirm</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R03.0</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting finding; superseded by the diagnosis at the six-week visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>Healed stab wound of the left chest, repaired by thoracotomy seven years ago; occasional aching along the scar with coughing and in cold weather, without exertional or ischemic features</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z87.828</td><td>S — Synthetic modern problem anchored to his documented stabbing and chest surgery in 1958.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-8">
    <td>Stage 1 hypertension (2017 ACC/AHA), confirmed by home readings averaging 136/86 mmHg; no end-organ damage (normal ECG, urine albumin, kidney function and fundi); low estimated 10-year risk; lifestyle treatment</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
