    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, responding (F32.1)</content>. PHQ-9 8, a 53 percent fall from 17: response. GAD-7 5. Repeat PC-PTSD-5 1, positive only for being on guard, which fits his real circumstances. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg; no increase needed.</item><item>Therapy every two weeks.</item><item>Safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Nicotine dependence, in early remission (F17.210)</content>. Smoke-free apart from one lapse after a threat. A second twelve-week course of varenicline lowers the risk of relapse in people who have quit. [S]<list><item>Continue varenicline 1 mg twice daily for a further twelve weeks.</item><item>A plan for threatening calls that does not involve cigarettes, practised in therapy.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Stage 1 hypertension (I10)</content>. Home average 132/84, falling with lifestyle changes and stopping smoking. [S]<list><item>Continue lifestyle treatment; recheck home readings before the next visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Insomnia disorder, improving (G47.00)</content>. Insomnia Severity Index 10; about six and a half hours a night. [S]<list><item>Keep the fixed rising time while travelling.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9</td><td>At least monthly during acute treatment; every 2 to 4 weeks in continuation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>8, a 53 percent fall from 17</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>GAD-7</td><td>Every 4 to 8 weeks during treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PTSD screen (PC-PTSD-5)</td><td>Repeat at about three months and if trauma symptoms emerge</td><td>Completed today</td><td>1: on guard only; no PTSD</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal ideation; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0. Safety plan reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Psychiatry follow-up</td><td>At about eight to twelve weeks</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Video review with Dr. Lindqvist-Bankole last month; plan unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and adverse-effect review</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No missed sertraline doses; nausea on varenicline has settled</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Smoking status after the quit date</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>One lapse in June; smoke-free since</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Insomnia Severity Index and sleep diary</td><td>Every visit during CBT for insomnia</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Insomnia Severity Index 10; about six and a half hours a night (score in the notes; no LOINC code used)</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Home blood pressure readings</td><td>A week before each visit while treatment is adjusted</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seven-day average 132/84</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Office blood pressure, weight and BMI</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>130/84 mmHg; weight 84.0 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sustainable work plan: a day off each week, two speeches a day at most, sleep window kept</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Day off kept most weeks; two-week break taken</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Depression remission (PHQ-9 below 5) by six months. In progress; target 2026-09-15 [S]</item><item>Sleep of at least six and a half hours on most nights, with an Insomnia Severity Index below 10. In progress; target 2026-09-15 [S]</item><item>Smoke-free, confirmed at every visit after the quit date. In progress; target 2026-11-30 [S]</item><item>Home blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg with lifestyle changes. In progress; target 2026-12-31 [S]</item><item>A sustainable schedule: one full day a week without work, no more than two speeches a day, and a two-week break in the summer. Outcome by 2026-07-14: Kept for six weeks; two-week break taken in July [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Clinical Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Depression Across Three Age Cohorts (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders, hypertension and hyperlipidemia monographs (2026); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); Tobacco Smoking Cessation in Adults, Including Pregnant Persons: Interventions (2021); Neuropsychiatric safety and efficacy of varenicline, bupropion, and nicotine patch in smokers with and without psychiatric disorders (EAGLES) (2016); 2017 ACC/AHA/AAPA/ABC/ACPM/AGS/APhA/ASH/ASPC/NMA/PCNA Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation, and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2017)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Review in nine weeks with repeat lipids. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-15: twenty-three-week review: remission, smoking, blood pressure and lipids. [S]</paragraph></text>

